# Sensitive Data Exposure via Exposed `.env` File

## Summary

An environment configuration file (`.env`) was found to be publicly accessible.

Environment files are commonly used to store application configuration and secrets. Depending on the application, an exposed `.env` file may contain sensitive information such as API keys, database credentials, SMTP credentials, application secrets, or other configuration values.

This finding was identified during authorized security research using search engine reconnaissance.

